# format/fx_bi (id 226): built-in format code strings, part 1. Entered from fx_init (199) with the
# boot caller's (LR, LP). One block write of 658 words at 0xCA00 (staging inside the compiled
# record area, which is empty at boot): 36 descriptors [F, start, end] (the last is 0 0 0), then
# the UTF-16 units of the 35 built-in codes. Saves (LR, LP) in AR2, AC2, sets AC1 = DP = 0xCA00
# and goes to fx_bil (227), which packs each string into the heap with fx_fin2 / fx_fin3 /
# fx_pack and stores its handle in FMT_TABLE[F] (fx_bi3, 229). The payload is the biases of a
# dense layer with no inputs (0 columns). Codes are Excel's en-US built-ins (ids 1..22, 37..49).
# Note: fx_general.md (built-in formats).
